// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/chart-from-a-library.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeChartFromALibrary(path: "/recipes/chart-from-a-library", title: "Draw a chart from a library — Recipes", description: "Draw a Chart.js chart on a page: load the library from a CDN, call it from a script of your own, and redraw the chart when the page's data changes.") {
    RecipeShell("Draw a chart from a library", summary: "A charting library such as Chart.js wants a canvas and gives back a chart object. This page hands a canvas to the library, shows new figures when the reader switches years, and destroys the chart when the page leaves. You need a WebFluent project, and the scripts below saved under its `src/`.", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "troubleshooting", label: "Troubleshooting"), Anchor(id: "variations", label: "Variations")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Place a custom element from a library", to: "/recipes/place-a-custom-element"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Call your own JavaScript", to: "/recipes/call-your-own-script"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Hand an element to a script", to: "/recipes/hand-an-element-to-a-script")], source: "md-docs/recipes/chart-from-a-library.md", how: true, hasVariations: true, project: { "src/sales-chart.js": #"// src/sales-chart.js
/**
 * A bar chart of `values`, one bar a quarter, drawn on `canvas`.
 * @param {HTMLCanvasElement} canvas
 * @param {number[]} values
 */
function drawSales(canvas, values) {
  return new Chart(canvas, {
    type: "bar",
    data: {
      labels: ["Q1", "Q2", "Q3", "Q4"],
      datasets: [{ label: "Sales", data: values }],
    },
  });
}

/**
 * Show new figures on a chart that `drawSales` made.
 * @param {Chart} chart
 * @param {number[]} values
 */
function showSales(chart, values) {
  chart.data.datasets[0].data = values;
  chart.update();
}
"#, "src/pages/ChartFromALibrary.wf": #"page Sales(path: "/sales", title: "Sales", description: "Sales by quarter, as a bar chart.") {
    state lastYear = false
    derived values: [Number] = if lastYear { [9, 14, 11, 13] } else { [12, 19, 7, 15] }

    Heading("Sales").h1
    Switch(bind: lastYear, label: "Show last year")
    Host(tag: "canvas", role: "img", aria-label: "Sales by quarter",
         mount: (canvas) => drawSales(canvas, values),
         update: (chart) => showSales(chart, values),
         cleanup: (chart) => chart.destroy())
}
"#, "webfluent.app.json": #"{
  "name": "chart-from-a-library",
  "meta": {
    "scripts": [
      "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.1/dist/chart.umd.min.js"
    ]
  }
}
"# }) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** the script `src/sales-chart.js` and the `meta.scripts` setting, both shown below.")
            CodeBlock(#"page Sales(path: "/sales", title: "Sales", description: "Sales by quarter, as a bar chart.") {
    state lastYear = false
    derived values: [Number] = if lastYear { [9, 14, 11, 13] } else { [12, 19, 7, 15] }

    Heading("Sales").h1
    Switch(bind: lastYear, label: "Show last year")
    Host(tag: "canvas", role: "img", aria-label: "Sales by quarter",
         mount: (canvas) => drawSales(canvas, values),
         update: (chart) => showSales(chart, values),
         cleanup: (chart) => chart.destroy())
}"#, title: "wf")
            Markdown("The page calls two functions of a plain script under `src/`, typed with JSDoc:")
            CodeBlock(#"// src/sales-chart.js
/**
 * A bar chart of `values`, one bar a quarter, drawn on `canvas`.
 * @param {HTMLCanvasElement} canvas
 * @param {number[]} values
 */
function drawSales(canvas, values) {
  return new Chart(canvas, {
    type: "bar",
    data: {
      labels: ["Q1", "Q2", "Q3", "Q4"],
      datasets: [{ label: "Sales", data: values }],
    },
  });
}

/**
 * Show new figures on a chart that `drawSales` made.
 * @param {Chart} chart
 * @param {number[]} values
 */
function showSales(chart, values) {
  chart.data.datasets[0].data = values;
  chart.update();
}"#, title: "js")
            Markdown("The library itself loads from a CDN, through `meta.scripts` in `webfluent.app.json`:")
            CodeBlock(#"{ "meta": {
    "scripts": ["https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.1/dist/chart.umd.min.js"]
} }"#, title: "json")
        }
        variations {
            Markdown("To pin the library to the exact file you tested, add its subresource integrity hash to `meta.integrity`, keyed by the same URL. The build writes it on the tag with `crossorigin=\"anonymous\"`, and a library from another origin without one draws a `D05` warning. The compiler never fetches the file to work the hash out; your CDN lists it, or compute it from a copy of the file:")

            Terminal(lines: [
                        Line(command: "openssl dgst -sha384 -binary chart.umd.min.js | openssl base64 -A")
                    ])

            Markdown("The other ways an entry in `meta.scripts` can load (`async`, after the page, as a module, or with `globals` your `.wf` code calls directly) are in [Load a library from a CDN](/recipes/library-from-a-cdn).")

        }
        Markdown("- **The library loads first.** The build links each `meta.scripts` entry with `<script defer>`, in order, before your own scripts and the compiled code, so `Chart` exists when `drawSales` runs. It also widens the Content-Security-Policy by the CDN's origin, so the policy that ships beside the page does not block the library. The compiler never fetches the file, so `.wf` code never calls `Chart` directly: your script does.\n- **Your script is a plain browser script.** The build copies `src/sales-chart.js` to `build/js/` as written and puts its top-level names in scope, so the page calls `drawSales` and `showSales` by name. Its JSDoc types each call: `values` must be a list of numbers, and a call with the wrong number of arguments is a `T10` error ([Call your own JavaScript](/recipes/call-your-own-script)). `Chart` and `HTMLCanvasElement` are types WebFluent does not know, so they read as `Any`.\n- **`Host` makes the canvas.** `Host(tag: \"canvas\", …)` is a bare node for somebody else's code. `role: \"img\"` and `aria-label:` give the chart a name a screen reader announces, since a canvas has no text.\n- **`mount:` draws the chart.** It runs when the canvas is made, and what it returns, the `Chart` object, is the handle `update:` and `cleanup:` receive ([Hand an element to a script](/recipes/hand-an-element-to-a-script)).\n- **`update:` follows the data.** It reads `values`, so it runs again whenever the switch changes `values`, and `showSales` gives the existing chart the new figures instead of drawing a new one.\n- **`cleanup:` destroys the chart** when the page leaves, so nothing the library set up outlives the canvas.")

        Heading("Troubleshooting", id: "troubleshooting").h2

        Table(caption: "Troubleshooting") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("What you see").header
                    Table.Cell("What to do").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`mount failed ReferenceError: Chart is not defined` in the console") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The library did not load: check the URL in `meta.scripts`, and that the page was rebuilt after the config changed") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("The chart draws once and never changes")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Make `update:` read the state the chart shows; an `update:` that reads nothing never runs again") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Two charts on one canvas after a route change")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Destroy the chart in `cleanup:`") }
                }
            }
        }

    }
}
